WEBVTT

00:20:59.079 --> 00:21:01.079
Talk a bit more about some
of the other uses of it,

00:21:01.079 --> 00:21:04.496
because one of the things that's most
surprising is it's not just about sort

00:21:04.496 --> 00:21:09.454
of text responses. It's it can take
generalized human instructions

00:21:09.454 --> 00:21:12.746
and build things up. For example,
you can say to it,

00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:17.246
write a Python program that
is designed to put

00:21:17.246 --> 00:21:20.579
a flashing cursor in one
corner of the screen,

00:21:20.579 --> 00:21:22.204
in the Google logo in the other corner.

00:21:22.496 --> 00:21:26.204
And and it can go your way and
do something like that.

00:21:26.413 --> 00:21:28.913
Shockingly, quite well, effectively.

00:21:29.371 --> 00:21:31.788
Yeah, I it can.